<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29793" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mūcĭdus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mucc-</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj.
		mucus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Mouldy, musty</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mucida panis frusta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					14, 128</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					8, 6, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Snivelling</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homo es, Qui me emunxisti mucidum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Epid. 3, 4, 58</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">senex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Mil. 3, 1, 52</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
